    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 now builds the code from three parts:\n- `CITY3`: upper-cased first three letters of the owner's city\n- `LAST3`: upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n- `NNNN`: a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence \u2014 one more than the number of owners already in that city (was a global count over all owners)\n\n**Everything derived from `customerCode` is automatically rebuilt on the new format** because it reads `owner.getCustomerCode()`:\n- `AssignMembershipNumber` produces `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, which now yields e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26` (updated its javadoc example accordingly).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` descriptions and examples to reflect the new format.\n\nTests: the new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
